<title>UK: LIFFE grains quiet, lower after long weekend.</title>
<headline>LIFFE grains quiet, lower after long weekend.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE wheat ended lower after a particularly quiet day.</p>
<p>Total volume on wheat was just 21 lots, with front month July most active with 10 lots changing hands. It last traded 0.55 stg lower at 89.70 stg.</p>
<p>There was no trade at all in barley.</p>
<p>Traders blamed the aftermath of the long weekend, and quiet fob and delivered markets. &quot;Nobody wanted to play,&quot; one said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
